plumes of smoke and blazing fire at an  oil depot in vasel cave about 40  kilometers south west of kiev  ukrainian media say the fire is the  result of a russian airstrike the  ukrainian capital itself has spent  another night under heavy artillery  bombardment  as the russian push to reach the city  intensifies  satellite imagery shows a 60 kilometer  column of russian tanks breaking away in  different directions in an attempt to  encircle the capital kiev is already  besieged from the north the east and the  west  now the russian army is trying to  complete the circle from the south  it is believed ground troops are 25  kilometers away from the heart of the  capital  on the morning of march 12 high  precision long-range weapons attacked  ukraine's military infrastructure  including the military airfield in vasil  kov and the main center of radio and  electronic intelligence of the ukrainian  armed forces in bravery in total during  the operation  3491 objects of the military  infrastructure of ukraine were disabled  the impact is visible across ukraine  including here in the eastern town of  volno  look we were sitting in basements and  they were walking around everywhere  shooting we couldn't leave the basement  for over a day then i walked up to a  soldier and i said boys my mum is  bedridden up there she's a grandma and i  can't go up there the guys wanted to  help me bring her down into the basement  but when we went up there she had  already died it was already too late  residential areas in kiev and mario paul  lie in ruins  the russian onslaught has also  intensified in northern eastern and  southern ukraine  bringing more death and destruction to  populated cities  ukraine has accused russian forces of  having kidnapped the mayor of melitopol  in the southeast of the country  protesters gathered in front of the  city's local government headquarters  demanding the release of the mayor  we demand the mayor be immediately  released we're talking to france germany  israel and others i personally have  called german chancellor schultz and  french president macron i'll talk to  everybody necessary in order to get our  people released we expect world leaders  to show how they can influence the  situation and do one simple thing get  this one person released the very person  that represents the people of militarpol  there have been several attempts at a  ceasefire while the human exodus within  and out of ukraine continues  today march 12 2022 we announced the  opening of the next humanitarian  corridors i very much hope that it will  be a good day all the planned routes  will be open and russia will abide by  its commitments to ceasefire guarantees  i will inform during the day about the  results of our humanitarian routes  these videos published by the head of  the zoporizia regional state  administration alexander starok on his  official telegram channel seemed to show  the progress of a column of buses and  red cross vehicles on their way to mario  paul from zapporusia on saturday  at least one million ukrainians have  been internally displaced by the war  while more than 2.5 million have been  forced to leave the country  muhammad al-jazeera
 

